  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.54,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.15,
    "rationale": "The OD plateaus at about 0.53 from 5 h to 18 h. A plateau like this could be detector saturation hiding continued growth, so I diluted the 18 h aliquot to test it. Dilution-corrected readings were: x2 gave 0.537, x5 gave 0.515, x10 gave 0.575 (two replicates), and x25 gave 0.61 (two replicates, noisy). The undiluted reading was 0.531. If the reader were saturating, the corrected values would rise steadily with dilution and sit well above 0.53. Here the x2 and x5 values match the undiluted reading, and the x10 and x25 values are only modestly higher and noisy. They are not a monotonic trend, since x5 is lower than x2. The x10 and x25 values fit replicate scatter at low OD, where the replicates differed by roughly 7–25%. The reader looks linear up to about 0.53, so the plateau is a real stationary phase."
  },
